ch in 1662. The rest of the statues on the facade are of prominent counts of the time.\n<p>You can take a peak on the inside during working hours, where you can see the stained-glass window of Jean Bart's return to the city after the struggle at Texel.<\/p><\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/09\/DSC_5049.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The Tour of Leughenaer is the city&#039;s oldest building. It served as a watch tower at the time. &lt;i&gt;Leughenaer&lt;\/i&gt; actually means liar in old Flemish. The building was likely named the lying tower as many ships mistook it for a light house and ended up stuck in the sand.\" data-attachment-id=\"4796\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The Tour of Leughenaer is the city&#039;s oldest building. It served as a watch tower at the time. &lt;i&gt;Leughenaer&lt;\/i&gt; actually means liar in old Flemish. The building was likely named the lying tower as many ships mistook it for a light house and ended up stuck in the sand.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/09\/DSC_5049\/797284865.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The Tour of Leughenaer is the city's oldest building. It served as a watch tower at the time. <i>Leughenaer<\/i> actually means liar in old Flemish. The building was likely named the lying tower as many ships mistook it for a light house and end