s\/2019\/09\/DSC_5148.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Can you guess to who&#039;s room this safety boat is closest to? The captain&#039;s of course! While captains are technically the last ones to leave the boat, who will notice in the commotion?\n&lt;p&gt;It is also interesting to note that the officers&#039; and captain&#039;s quarters are located at the back of the ship because there is a lot less turbulence at the back.&lt;\/p&gt;\" data-attachment-id=\"4837\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Can you guess to who&#039;s room this safety boat is closest to? The captain&#039;s of course! While captains are technically the last ones to leave the boat, who will notice in the commotion?\n&lt;p&gt;It is also interesting to note that the officers&#039; and captain&#039;s quarters are located at the back of the ship because there is a lot less turbulence at the back.&lt;\/p&gt;\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/09\/DSC_5148\/2641845147.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Can you guess to who's room this safety boat is closest to? The captain's of course! While captains are technically the last ones to leave the boat, who will notice in the commotion?\n<p>It is also interesting to note that the officers' and captain's quarters are located at the back of the ship because there is a lot less turbulence at the back.<\/p><\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/09\/DSC_5147.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Next door to the &lt;i&gt;Duchesse Anne&lt;\/i&gt; is the &lt;i&gt;Sandettie&lt;\/i&gt;, built in 1947 at Le Havre. With its distinct bright red color, the &lt;i&gt;Sandettie&lt;\/i&gt; was easily recognizable as a lightship. It served to announce the edge of a sand dune in order to help ships avoid getting stuck. Because it was very important for these ships to stay in one particular location, they had 13-ton anchors. That is twice the size of that of the &lt;i&gt;Duchesse Anne&lt;\/i&gt; even though this ship is half the other&#039;s size!\" data-attachment-id=\"4836\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Next door to the &lt;i&gt;Duchesse Anne&lt;\/i&gt; is the &lt;i&gt;Sandettie&lt;\/i&gt;, built in 1947 at Le Havre. With its distinct bright red color, the &lt;i&gt;Sandettie&lt;\/i&gt; was easily recognizable as a lightship. It served to announce the edge of a sand dune in order to help ships avoid getting stuck. Because it was very important for these ships to stay in one particular location, they had 13-ton anchors. That is twice the size of that of the &lt;i&gt;Duchesse Anne&lt;\/i&gt; even though this ship is half the other&#039;s size!\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/09\/DSC_5147\/3784057727.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Next door to the <i>Duchesse Anne<\/i> is the <i>Sandettie<\/i>, built in 1947 at Le Havre. With its distinct bright red color, the <i>Sandettie<\/i> was easily recognizable as a lightship. It served to announce the edge of a sand dune in order to help ships avoid getting stuck. Because it was very important for these ships to stay in one particular location, they had 13-ton anchors. That is twice the size of that of the <i>Duchesse Anne<\/i> even though this ship is half the other's size!<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/09\/DSC_5140.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Lightships were recognizable by day due to the red color and by night due to the beacon at the top. The light from this beacon could reach up to 46km!\" data-attachment-id=\"4832\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Lightships were recognizable by day due to the red color and by night due to the beacon at the top. The light from this beacon could reach up to 46km!\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2019\/09\/DSC_5140\/297240965.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Lightships were recognizable by day due to the red color and by night due to the beacon at the top. The light from this beacon could reach up to 46km!<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/09\/20190908_161115.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"To pre